{"total_count":10,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/594","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/594/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/594/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/594/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/594","id":190210609,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxOTAyMTA2MDk=","number":594,"title":"Error: Ensure that there are not multiple versions of GraphQL installed in your node_modules directory","user":{"login":"richburdon","id":3523355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjMzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3523355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon","html_url":"https://github.com/richburdon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richburdon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":42,"created_at":"2016-11-18T01:09:32Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T08:52:19Z","closed_at":"2017-08-17T21:14:50Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"[Related to https://github.com/graphql/graphiql/issues/58]\r\n\r\nI have two node modules A => B, where B creates a GraphQLSchema object that is imported by A, which is then used to instantiate graphqlExpress.\r\n\r\nI get this error:\r\n`\r\nEnsure that there are not multiple versions of GraphQL installed in your node_modules directory\r\n`\r\n\r\nAnd see that I have 2 different instances of the GraphQLSchema class type at runtime -- so validate.js invariant(schema instanceof GraphQLSchema) fails because the imported schema is an instance of A's GraphQLSchema not B's GraphQLSchema.\r\n\r\nHowever, all npm dependencies are of the same version (in both A and B modules).\r\n\r\n```\r\n> npm --version\r\n3.10.7\r\n\r\n> babel-node --version\r\n6.16.0\r\n\r\n> find node_modules -name graphql\r\nnode_modules/graphql\r\nnode_modules/graphql-subscriptions/node_modules/graphql\r\n\r\n> grep version node_modules/graphql/package.json \r\n0.7.2\r\n\r\n> grep version node_modules/graphql-subscriptions/node_modules/graphql/package.json\r\n0.7.2\r\n```\r\n\r\nI assume this is a common pattern, but I can't find an example.\r\n\r\nBTW, I'm using npm-link to create the A => B dependency.\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/594/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/594/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1539","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1539/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1539/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1539/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1539","id":365703462,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNjU3MDM0NjI=","number":1539,"title":"Throwing error inside Subscription resolver","user":{"login":"DBL-Lee","id":8804410,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MDQ0MTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8804410?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee","html_url":"https://github.com/DBL-Lee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DBL-Lee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":230677111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzA2NzcxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/labels/question","name":"question","color":"cc317c","default":true,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2018-10-02T01:24:30Z","updated_at":"2020-06-05T10:22:29Z","closed_at":"2020-06-03T19:22:11Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"/label question\r\n\r\nI would like to check for some permission before user subscribe to an endpoint. An error should be thrown and the client should be able to catch the error.\r\n\r\nThe following is what I am trying:\r\n\r\n```\r\nsomeSubscriptionEndpoint: {\r\n\tsubscribe: (payload, args, context, info) => {\r\n\t\tthrow new Error('Internal server error');\r\n         }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut the error I receive on client side is `\"Subscription field must return Async Iterable. Received: [object Object]\"`\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/blob/master/src/subscription/subscribe.js#L272\r\n\r\nThis line is called twice, the first time eventStream is the error I threw so condition is true and the error is wrapped and rethrown. The second time I received  `{ errors: [ [GraphQLError] ] }` and the the error in line 281 is thrown.\r\n\r\nWhat is the correct way of throwing an error when client subscribes to an specific subscription endpoint?\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1539/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1539/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1202","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1202/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1202/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1202/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1202","id":287766721,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyODc3NjY3MjE=","number":1202,"title":"Issues with the dedent string tag used for testing","user":{"login":"Cito","id":464599,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NDU5OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/464599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito","html_url":"https://github.com/Cito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2018-01-11T12:18:47Z","updated_at":"2018-01-18T19:54:43Z","closed_at":"2018-01-18T19:54:43Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"GraphQL.js has a ES6 string tag helper function under `jsutils/dedent` that removes indentation from strings so that the unit tests can look nicer.\r\n\r\nOne undocumented side effect of the `dedent` function however confused me when reading some of the tests: The tag also adds escape sequences to the dedented string. Take for example this test:\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n  it('Prints String Field With String Arg With Default', () => {\r\n    const output = printSingleFieldSchema({\r\n      type: GraphQLString,\r\n      args: { argOne: { type: GraphQLString, defaultValue: 'tes\\t de\\fault' } },\r\n    });\r\n    expect(output).to.equal(dedent`\r\n      schema {\r\n        query: Root\r\n      }\r\n\r\n      type Root {\r\n        singleField(argOne: String = \"tes\\t de\\fault\"): String\r\n      }\r\n    `);\r\n  });\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe output actually contains escape sequences, like `\"tes\\\\t de\\\\fault\"`, but the test looks likes as if it expects the output to be a non-escaped string.\r\n\r\nThe reason for this is that the `dedent` tag accesses `string.raw` instead of `string`.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure whether this is intended or not. If it *is*, then it should at least be documented in `jsutils/dedent`, because having such a side effect is not what you expect from a function called \"dedent\". It should also be documented that the function only looks at spaces, it does *not* dedent tab-based indentation.\r\n\r\nIf you me know whether you prefer fixing the documentation or fixing the behavior, I can create a PR.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1202/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1202/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1027","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1027/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1027/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1027/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/1027","id":255935130,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0MTM5ODAzNTk4","number":1027,"title":"Add missing ExecutionArgs export","user":{"login":"IvanGoncharov","id":8336157,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMzYxNTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8336157?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov","html_url":"https://github.com/IvanGoncharov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IvanGoncharov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":231582573,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzE1ODI1NzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/labels/CLA%20Signed","name":"CLA Signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2017-09-07T13:22:29Z","updated_at":"2017-12-14T18:20:10Z","closed_at":"2017-09-08T22:45:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/pulls/1027","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/1027","diff_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/1027.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/1027.patch","merged_at":"2017-09-08T22:45:35Z"},"body":"In #988 I forget to export `ExecutionArgs` in all necessary places 🤦‍♂️ \r\nThis one-line PR fix that. \r\n@wincent Can you please review it?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1027/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1027/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1141","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1141/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1141/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1141/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/1141","id":281872713,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0MTU4MTg2NTk5","number":1141,"title":"Add experimental support for parsing variable definitions in fragments","user":{"login":"sam-swarr","id":16216174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16216174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr","html_url":"https://github.com/sam-swarr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sam-swarr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":231582573,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzE1ODI1NzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/labels/CLA%20Signed","name":"CLA Signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":14,"created_at":"2017-12-13T19:45:35Z","updated_at":"2018-07-20T13:43:02Z","closed_at":"2017-12-14T20:50:44Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/pulls/1141","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/1141","diff_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/1141.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/1141.patch","merged_at":"2017-12-14T20:50:44Z"},"body":"This PR adds experimental support for parsing variable definitions within a fragment declaration. If the `fragmentVariablesExperimental` flag is passed into the options for `parse` then the parser will accept `VariableDefinitions` placed after the `TypeCondition` and before any `Directives`. The syntax is identical to the usual query-defined variable definitions, and the parser will parse these into the optional `variableDefinitions` field on `FragmentDefinitionNode`.\r\n\r\nContext:\r\nThere's been ongoing discussion on exploring this concept: https://github.com/facebook/graphql/issues/204. Note that this PR only supports parsing fragment variable definitions into the AST. It does not allow for passing variable values into a fragment spread. It at least gets a foot in the door for starting to explore further down this path.\r\n\r\nAn emergent pain point with the current system (where a query must define all variables used in its dependent fragments) is that adding a new variable reference to a commonly used fragment could involve updating the declarations of the dozens of queries that depend on that fragment. With this PR, it would become easy to implement a client side transform that would allow for variable defaults defined at the fragment level to be automatically hoisted to its dependent queries. For example, with\r\n\r\n```\r\nquery q () {\r\n  ...a\r\n}\r\n\r\nfragment a on t ($size: Int = 0) {\r\n  f(size: $size)\r\n}\r\n```\r\nthe transform would automatically hoist the `$size` variable declaration into `query q` without the need to explicitly define it. This can be useful if `fragment a` is used by many queries.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1141/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":5,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/1141/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/951","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/951/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/951/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/951/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/951","id":243459935,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0MTMwOTAyNzUz","number":951,"title":"Fix incorrect column number in errors","user":{"login":"dwwoelfel","id":476818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NjgxOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/476818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel","html_url":"https://github.com/dwwoelfel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":231582573,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzE1ODI1NzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/labels/CLA%20Signed","name":"CLA Signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2017-07-17T16:55:22Z","updated_at":"2017-07-17T17:12:29Z","closed_at":"2017-07-17T17:00:29Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/pulls/951","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/951","diff_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/951.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/951.patch","merged_at":"2017-07-17T17:00:29Z"},"body":"I forgot to check that we were on the first line before applying the column offset to the caret in #951 951. It causes the indicator and reported column number for the error to be off if a locationOffset.column is larger than 1.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/951/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/951/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/949","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/949/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/949/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/949/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/949","id":242878070,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0MTMwNTAyNjE3","number":949,"title":"Account for query's offset in file for errors","user":{"login":"dwwoelfel","id":476818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NjgxOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/476818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel","html_url":"https://github.com/dwwoelfel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dwwoelfel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":231582573,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzE1ODI1NzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/labels/CLA%20Signed","name":"CLA Signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2017-07-14T02:10:12Z","updated_at":"2017-07-14T20:56:58Z","closed_at":"2017-07-14T20:56:57Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/pulls/949","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/949","diff_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/949.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/949.patch","merged_at":"2017-07-14T20:56:57Z"},"body":"Adds support for providing the location in a file that the graphQL source was located. If the location is provided as part of the source, the line numbers in the formatted errors will be updated to account for the offset.\r\n\r\nFor example, in file Foo.js:\r\n\r\n```\r\n1  const x = 1\r\n2 \r\n3  graphql`\r\n4  query {\r\n5   ?\r\n6  }\r\n7  `\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe lexer will throw an error with message:\r\n\r\n```\r\nParse error: GraphQLError: Syntax Error Foo.js (5:2) Cannot parse the unexpected character \"?\".\r\n4: query {\r\n5:  ?\r\n    ^\r\n6: }\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt's up to the caller to provide the correct offset in the source.\r\n\r\nNot sure if `location` is the best name for the field in the `Source` object. Very open to suggestions!","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/949/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/949/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/926","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/926/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/926/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/926/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/926","id":237697462,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0MTI2ODg1NDg3","number":926,"title":"RFC: Block String","user":{"login":"leebyron","id":50130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron","html_url":"https://github.com/leebyron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":231582573,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzE1ODI1NzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/labels/CLA%20Signed","name":"CLA Signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":31,"created_at":"2017-06-22T00:03:30Z","updated_at":"2017-11-30T17:13:46Z","closed_at":"2017-11-30T05:00:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/pulls/926","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/926","diff_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/926.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/926.patch","merged_at":"2017-11-30T05:00:21Z"},"body":"This RFC adds a new lexed token, the block string, similar to that found in Coffeescript, Python, and Scala.\r\n\r\nA block string starts and ends with a triple-quote:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"\"\"This is a triple-quoted string\r\nand it can contain multiple lines\"\"\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nBlock strings are useful for typing literal bodies of text where new lines should be interpreted literally. In fact, the only escape sequence used is `\\\"\"\"` and `\\` is otherwise allowed unescaped. This is beneficial when writing documentation within strings which may reference the back-slash often:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"\"\"\r\nIn a block string \\n and C:\\\\ are unescaped.\r\n\"\"\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe primary value of block strings are to write long-form input directly in query text, in tools like GraphiQL, and as a prerequisite to another pending RFC to allow docstring style documentation in the Schema Definition Language.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/926/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":6,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/926/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/977","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/977/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/977/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/977/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/977","id":247168377,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNDcxNjgzNzc=","number":977,"title":"resolve() function changes the data type of arg from int to string","user":{"login":"need47","id":1194165,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTQxNjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1194165?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47","html_url":"https://github.com/need47","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/need47/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2017-08-01T18:59:28Z","updated_at":"2017-08-01T19:05:50Z","closed_at":"2017-08-01T19:05:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I have the following working code. I started the server (using express and express-graphql) and tried the query below:\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  user(id: 1) {\r\n    id\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nI go the response:\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"data\": {\r\n    \"user\": {\r\n      \"id\": \"1\"\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nI found the type of id changed from integer to string. Also please note the the console.log() line. The arg `id` became string in the first place. \r\n\r\n```js\r\n//\r\n// type and schema\r\n//\r\nimport {\r\n  GraphQLSchema,\r\n  GraphQLObjectType,\r\n  GraphQLID,\r\n  GraphQLString,\r\n  GraphQLNonNull,\r\n  GraphQLList\r\n} from 'graphql';\r\n\r\nconst User = new GraphQLObjectType({\r\n  name: 'User',\r\n  fields: () => ({\r\n    id: {\r\n      type: GraphQLID\r\n    }\r\n })\r\n});\r\n\r\nconst Query = new GraphQLObjectType({\r\n  name: 'Query',\r\n  fields: () => ({\r\n    user: {\r\n      type: User,\r\n      args: {\r\n        id: {\r\n          type: new GraphQLNonNull(GraphQLID) // integer\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      resolve: (parent, { id }) => {\r\n        console.log('type: ', typeof id); // string\r\n        return {id: id};\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  })\r\n});\r\n\r\nconst Schema = new GraphQLSchema({\r\n  query: Query\r\n});\r\n\r\n//\r\n// server\r\n//\r\nimport express from 'express';\r\nimport graphqlHTTP from 'express-graphql';\r\n\r\nvar app = express();\r\napp.use('/graphql', graphqlHTTP({\r\n  schema: Schema,\r\n  graphiql: true,\r\n}));\r\napp.listen(4000, () => {\r\n  console.log('Running a GraphQL API server at localhost:4000/graphql')\r\n});\r\n```\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/977/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/977/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/427","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/427/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/427/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/427/events","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/427","id":164683436,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0NzY4NTU4NzA=","number":427,"title":"parse comments beginning with `##` as descriptions on schema definitions","user":{"login":"charlieschwabacher","id":533045,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMzA0NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/533045?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher","html_url":"https://github.com/charlieschwabacher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlieschwabacher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":231582573,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzE1ODI1NzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/labels/CLA%20Signed","name":"CLA Signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":17,"created_at":"2016-07-09T20:08:23Z","updated_at":"2016-08-25T23:06:33Z","closed_at":"2016-08-24T20:45:13Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/pulls/427","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/427","diff_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/427.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/pull/427.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This pull adds a comment syntax for descriptions to the schema definition language as discussed in https://github.com/facebook/graphql/pull/90.\n\nThe details of the comment syntax have not been worked out in that thread - if there is something you prefer vs these 'double hash' comments, I'm happy to update.\n\nAs this pull stands, comments beginning with a second hash mark (`##`) will be parsed as description AST nodes and attached to the following type or field definition.\n\nfor example:\n\n``` graphql\n## description of type 'User'\ntype User {\n  ## description of field 'firstName'\n  firstName: String\n}\n```\n\nchanges to lexer:\n- when the lexer encounters a `#` character, it checks the next char - if that is also a `#`, it takes text from the current position to the end of the line and produces a `DESCRIPTION` token.\n\nchanges to parser:\n- when parsing top level definitions, before looking at the initial keyword, the parser first takes any number of `DESCRIPTION` tokens, joins their values, and creates a description AST node.  Then it takes the keyword - if the definition is an `OperationDefinition` or `FragmentDefinition` the description is discarded.  If the definition is a `TypeSystemDefinition` the description node is attached to the definition node.\n- when parsing field, input value, or enum value definitions, if there are any leading `DESCRIPTION` tokens, the parser creates a `Description` node and attaches it to the final `FieldDefinition`, `InputValueDefinition`, or `EnumValueDefinition` node.\n\nchanges to buildASTSchema.js:\n- descriptions on AST nodes are attached to Type objects.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/427/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/427/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}